This is a simple test to see if I can setup and use an XBox One controller with the Q:
More about this on the Arduino forum thread: 
https://forum.arduino.cc/t/anyone-had-luck-reading-from-a-gamepad/1436918


I started up the Q as stand alone and went to the bluetooth app, where I did a scan and then a did a bind
to my Joystick... Took a few attempts.

I then used the instuctions that the @ptillish (Arduino Forum) on being able to setup the python on the Q
to include other packages like pygame.

https://forum.arduino.cc/t/uno-q-possible-to-connect-python-not-containerized-with-arduino/1436102/8


Instructions on how once I have things setup how I program the Arduino side, if needed:
    arduino-cli compile --fqbn arduino:zephyr:unoq --upload sketch/

And how to start up the python within uv framework:
    Python: uv run python/main.py
